 "summary": "IBM scripting and macro language designed by Mike Cowlishaw in which every value is a character string, with decimal arithmetic of arbitrary precision, compound (stem) variables as associative arrays, PARSE templates and an ADDRESS instruction for driving host command environments; standardized as ANSI X3.274-1996.",
