 ],
 "level_notes": {
  "0": "Main open implementations: Regina (portable C interpreter, SourceForge), ooRexx (Object Rexx, open-sourced by IBM, SourceForge SVN) and BREXX; IBM's z/OS and z/VM interpreters are proprietary.",
  "1": "ANSI X3.274-1996 (X3J18) is the standard; the RexxLA hosts the public committee draft. Cowlishaw's book 'The Rexx Language' (TRL1 1985, TRL2 1990) is the original definition. ooRexx reference documents the object-oriented superset.",
  "3": "Rosetta Code reports 'blocked' to automated checkers."
